{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And he set him before Pharaoh.</b> The reason for his saying <b>וַיַּעֲמִידֵהוּ</b> etc. — perhaps it is that he set him in the place of Joseph, for Pharaoh had assigned him a place before his throne, when he said to him (Genesis 41:40): ״רַק הַכִּסֵּא אֶגְדַּל מִמֶּךָּ״, and the verse informs us that Joseph set his father before Pharaoh in the most esteemed place, close to the king." "<b>Further,</b> it may intend that he set him opposite his face, in the manner of those who bless, and Jacob blessed etc." "<b>Further,</b> it may intend to inform that there was a need to set him before him, because Pharaoh was low of stature and short in height (Mo'ed Katan 18b); it was necessary to identify him to him, so he set him before him to say, 'This is he.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {0 "The Talmudic citation in comment [2] (מועד קטן יח.) refers to Mo'ed Katan 18b, where Pharaoh is described as short of stature."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:49:26.933861466Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}